WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.400
[Wren] Nick, remember how I had to take that Uber yesterday to get to work?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.400
It was because my car wouldn't start!

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:17.159
I almost didn't make it to work today, I almost had to take another Uber.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.540
So this is the Boosted Board. It's an amazing piece of equipment

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.400
You may recognize it from Mario Skate that we shot a couple years ago

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.200
What if I actually rode this work instead of driving this car?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.200
My issue is that this boosted board tops out at about five miles of range, whereas I live about 15 miles away.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.250
I've actually seen videos of people who have modified their boosted boards by putting extra battery packs on them.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.900
You want to consider the right battery to use, and the first obvious choice is a lithium polymer battery

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.600
Known as a LiPo. These are commonly used in like drones and RC cars and stuff like that today

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.820
But what peaked my interest is this 18650 battery made by Panasonic. And what makes this thing special

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.020
Is that this is the exact battery used today to power the world's most technologically advanced cars on the market.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.000
Yeah what's the name of your car?

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:57.940
[Brandon] Geoffrey

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.780
[Wren] Geoffrey?! Haha!

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.340
[Brandon] The one true king!

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.380
[Wren] So you have a P85d which has exactly

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.820
7,100 Batteries inside and the way, it's arranged. Is that you have basically

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.300
16 modules of like

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.420
444 Batteries

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.720
oh

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:25.680
Man that does not get old that's incredible. The batteries in this car are designed to hold a lot of energy, but not output that

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.630
energy very fast. All right, so imagine

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:34.960
That this glass of water represents the Boosted Board battery which is a lithium iron phosphate battery, and that this bottle of water

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.770
represents the Panasonic Batteries found inside Tesla cars

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:41.850
which is the lithium Nickel cobalt aluminum dioxide battery.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:48.360
With the water inside both representing electrical energy. This one for instance can pour all the water out really really fast

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:54.990
Oh but look, now this glass of water is empty. No more water. This one even though it holds a lot more water

00:01:55.030 --> 00:02:00.330
it takes a lot longer to pour it all out because it can't pour it out that fast. You got this bottleneck here.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.120
If I wanted to make this pour out water faster

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.960
how do I do that? Well the answer is to add another bottle of water in parallel.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.820
So what happens is that with both of these pouring at the same time, you have double the output rate of water!

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:18.030
So much water now! Why use a smaller amount of water when you can have a lot of water and output just as fast?

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.440
If these batteries can actually power this massive car to go so fast,

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.480
surely having a couple packs in parallel on my Boosted Board will be able to deliver the power

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.500
I need and the longevity that I also need to get to work. [Brandon] You're gonna ride all that way to work?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.300
[Wren] Yeah dude, it's like 15 miles away.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.200
[Brandon] Oh man.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:41.610
[Wren] Yeah. Hopefully, it works! My plan is to make a battery pack that matches the voltage of the Boosted Board itself which is about 40 volts

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:47.190
I have to take each of these 10, connect them end to end and then take the second 10, and also connect those end to end.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.410
This will give me two packs of 10 batteries each that will connect in parallel to double the output rate and the

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.339
capacity. We have the battery pack right here, and we have the control board.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.739
This is where all the circuitry goes and if I lift this off,

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:00.040
you'll see

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.090
exactly what I'm talking about.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:06.540
So what I'm going to do is I'm going to splice the batteries directly into the cables where they meet at the control board. AKA,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.869
I have to solder wires directly to the board. I could destroy this $1500 piece of equipment

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.060
and I don't think warranty will cover this.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.889
What I'm doing here is making custom bullet connectors that I can connect the batteries directly to the Boosted Board itself

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:31.040
I've made two bullet connectors on wire. This plate actually covers the control board and I'm going to drill a hole

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.630
straight through this so that I can take these connectors which connect to the battery and will stick out of it.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.820
And then I'll get the right length

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:41.440
And then I'll snip these here and solder the ends of these onto the control board. That'll do wonderfully.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.720
And be able to pull this up and over. Oh man

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.420
look at that

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:55.130
Here are the two wires we're most concerned with. I'm actually going to cut a small little hole to expose this wire and

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.229
expose this wire. From there, I'll be able to take these and solder them directly to the cable.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:05.749
This is actually the part most nervous about simply because I'm officially voiding the warranty now. Uh, hopefully this thing doesn't break.

00:04:05.749 --> 00:04:09.640
I think it works man. These things are stuck on there. They are not coming off.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.600
There's now exposed connectors here, so I'm going to cover that up with liquid tape which is essentially just electrical tape

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:21.460
but fluid. The last step of this mod is to create these little Y connectors, little splitters here that will connect the batteries together and

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.470
into the Boosted Board as a single stream of power.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:34.189
[Nick] What's up? [Wren] We have an issue, that I probably should've checked on first. I let the Boosted Board bit, get too

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.279
low on energy and then I just let it sit there for, months.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.690
Over time battery's kind of lose their charge and now the battery charge has gotten too

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.760
low in the Boosted Board to even turn on and if I plug it in green light comes on, red charging,

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.560
[Confused Wren] and now it's blinking.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:52.880
And there is a way to fix this dead battery problem. We need to borrow your car.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.999
By towing myself behind Nick's car

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:03.880
I turn the motors into power generators which add enough energy into the battery to revive it and allow it to be charged again.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.640
Oh God. Ah! Ah! Ugh!

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.160
I'm going to try it.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.060
Yes! It turned on.

00:05:13.399 --> 00:05:19.059
The board has been charging for last half-hour. Now the moment of truth is to see if it turns on.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.000
Hey, okay, it's green. Solid green. That means it's on. Does it connect?

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:28.540
Yes!

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:30.020
It works!

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.300
Just do it!

00:05:35.179 --> 00:05:36.949
I'm light-headed now.

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:38.949
We fixed it Nick! Dude

00:05:39.409 --> 00:05:43.479
I got this incredibly strong, Velcro. So if I just pop this on...

00:05:44.749 --> 00:05:52.058
We got this guy. These two batteries are connected together and into the Boosted Board. We're good. Seems to be working.

00:06:00.549 --> 00:06:03.599
[Nick] How can you tell the range. That is a bit of an issue?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.480
There is no way to tell the range. The only way to know is to test it.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:13.320
I'm excited. So for all intents and purposes, this is where I'm starting, very close to Griffith Park here in Burbank

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:18.300
slash, Glendale area and I'm going to be going down along this bike path right next to the LA river.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.620
I am now driving right alongside I-5 here,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.020
and look at traffic.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.100
I'm going the same speed...

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.060
...kind of.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:43.320
I'm approximately two to three miles away from where I started. Normally I'd be halfway through a Boosted Board battery even though it says that I'm basically dead.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.480
So far that is the scariest part about this mod. Is that I have no way of

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:54.600
actively monitoring what my battery levels are so that's a bit scary. This is it. If I take one more step

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.300
I'll be the farthest away from home I've ever been.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:04.040
Come on Sam. Remember what Bilbo used to say. A good half of this entire ride is right along this river

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.529
I'm just going to keep riding along this river as far as I can go.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.960
Well that sucks.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:22.160
Should I just say screw it and go past it? There is a worker over there. He might stop me. I think I'm pretty fast I might be able to, get around them.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:23.500
Just

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.060
continue on.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.000
I think I'm okay

00:07:32.249 --> 00:07:34.249
What an annoyance

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:38.088
So this fine gentleman basically just told me I can't continue this way because

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:42.020
of all the flooding, there's all this stuff that you got to chop down is that right?

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.180
[Worker] Yeah.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.440
[Wren] He's go a GoPro on me too, so

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.480
unfortunately, I have to turn around and go back. I don't know how far. How far do you think that is?

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.360
